"""The vendor's GLOBAL attribute-id table -- generated, do not edit.

Generated by `tools/re/gen_attr_ids.py` from the bundled profiles' `changeParas` sections.

674 names, **zero collisions**, and of the 244 names declared by more than one
device class every one agrees. That is what makes these ids *global*, unlike the
single-parameter `5Dxx` registry, which is per class -- the same number is `volume` on one
appliance class and a setpoint on another.

These address the `6C01` changed-parameter report and its documented siblings `4C01` (read)
and `5C01` (multi-attribute write).

⚠️ **A number here is not permission to write it.** No published model declares an operation
for any of those commands (all 1,451 products enumerated) and no appliance has been observed
accepting one. This is the table such a test would need, not evidence that it passes.
"""
